# Same range cuts as the DC3/DC4 sources (optimizes sim time):
DefaultRangeCut 0.005
Region Spacecraft
Spacecraft.Volume SCbody
Spacecraft.RangeCut 1.

Region Pipebody
Pipebody.Volume PIPbody
Pipebody.RangeCut 1.

DetectorTimeConstant 0.000002

# Distant particle event: bremsstrahlung from electrons (exp(-E/500 keV)) precipitating
# over 90000 km2 at 10 deg Earth-central angle (1272 km away, zenith 119.5 deg,
# azimuth 0 deg from north). Peak precipitating flux 9.2e+03 e/cm2/s above 50 keV.
# Peak photon flux at COSI 0.255 ph/cm2/s; Flux below is the lightcurve-averaged value.
# Rocking +21.88 deg, yaw -42.34 deg. Direction in detector frame.
DataChallenge.Source R2_DISTPAR0008
R2_DISTPAR0008.ParticleType 1
R2_DISTPAR0008.Beam FarFieldGaussian 97.654 317.660 6.759
R2_DISTPAR0008.Spectrum File R2_DISTPAR0008_spectrum.dat
R2_DISTPAR0008.Flux 0.0703995
# Light-curve times are relative to t_ref = 1835555205.0 (unix s, first orientation row of this burst).
# Simulate with DC3_final_530km_3_month_with_slew_15sbins_GalacticEarth_cut_normed.ori and add t_ref to the simulated times afterwards.
# Original light curve (absolute unix times): R2_DISTPAR0008_lightcurve.dat; see sim_time_reference.txt.
R2_DISTPAR0008.Lightcurve File false R2_DISTPAR0008_lightcurve_shifted.dat
R2_DISTPAR0008.EarthOccultation false
